NAME
  dup, dup2 - KNUCK syscalls

SYNOPSIS
  dup(fd)
  dup2(fd, newfd)

DESCRIPTION
  dup duplicates an open file descriptor (file, pipe, socket, device) to the
  lowest free descriptor number. dup2 duplicates it to a specific descriptor
  number, closing newfd first if it is open. The duplicate shares the same
  underlying open file description: same offset, same socket, same pipe end.

  dup2(fd, fd) is a no-op returning fd.

RETURN VALUES
  dup: new descriptor number, or nil,err
  dup2: newfd on success, or nil,err

ERRORS
  bad fd            fd is not open
  too many open files  no free descriptor slot (dup)

SEE ALSO
  open close pipe socket

KNUCK(2) manual page. Part of the KNUCK kernel distribution.